WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Let's move on to the second half of the 30 to 2 ratio, giving breaths.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Rescue breaths provide the fresh oxygen that the blood needs to carry to the brain.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
But before we begin, make sure you have a barrier device at your disposal.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Your instructor should have handed them out.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
It could be a CPR pocket mask or a face shield.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
We always use these when possible to protect both you and the patient.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
We'll review the steps now as your instructor demonstrates.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Step one is to open the airway by performing a head tilt, chin lift.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Without opening the airway, air cannot reach the lungs

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
because the tongue often blocks the back of the throat in an unresponsive person.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
To perform a head tilt, chin lift,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.000
place one hand on the forehead to tilt the head back

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.000
and use the fingers of your other hand to lift the chin upward.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Step two is delivering the breaths.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
While keeping the airway open,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.000
use your thumb and index finger to pinch the nose completely closed.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Place your mask or mouth over theirs to create a tight seal and give two rescue breaths.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.000
Each breath should last about one second.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.000
The most important thing to watch for is visible chest rise.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.000
You aren't trying to blow as hard as you can.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.000
You just want to see that chest move up and down.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.000
If you don't see the chest rise on the first try,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.000
reposition the head and attempt a second breath.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.000
If it still doesn't rise, don't keep trying.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Immediately go back to your 30 compressions

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.000
and try the breaths again after that set is done.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Remember, we must never interrupt our compressions for more than 10 seconds to give these breaths.

